  "result": "Shell completion now handles arguments containing `#`. The cause was in `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py`. It uses `shlex`, which by default treats `#` as the start of a comment and drops everything after it. I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` so `#` is kept as a normal character.\n\nA quick check on `prog a#b #c x` now returns `['prog', 'a#b', '#c', 'x']`. The existing tests in `tests/test_shell_completion.py` pass (58). I didn't add a regression test for `#` or a `CHANGES.md` entry, so say if you want them.",
